export const title = "AI App Preset Setup Guide";
export const html = "<h1>AI App Preset Setup Guide</h1>\n      <hr class=\"rule\" />\n      <p>In AI App Preset settings, you configure which AI apps apply to each preset, so the device runs a different AI app configuration depending on which preset is active.</p>\n\n      <h2>Enabling AI App Preset Mode</h2>\n      <div class=\"figure\">\n      <div class=\"app-window\">\n        <div class=\"app-topnav\">\n          <div class=\"app-logo\">&#9679; Indo AI <span style=\"font-weight:400;opacity:.7;\">AI Bridge</span></div>\n          <div>&#9776; &nbsp; Device 1C0610</div>\n          <div class=\"app-right\"><span class=\"btn small\">&#9675; Arm</span><span class=\"btn small primary\">&#9899; Disarm</span> <span class=\"btn small\">&#9633; Video Preview</span> admin &#9660;</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"app-body\">\n          <div class=\"app-sidebar-nav\">\n            <div class=\"grp\">Record Setting</div>\n            <div class=\"item\">Recording &#9656;</div>\n            <div class=\"grp\">System Settings</div>\n            <div class=\"item\">Network &#9656;</div>\n            <div class=\"item\">System &#9656;</div>\n            <div class=\"item\">License Management</div>\n            <div class=\"item\">Integrations</div>\n            <div class=\"grp\">App Settings</div>\n            <div class=\"item\">Explore AI Apps</div>\n            <div class=\"item\">Active AI Apps &#9656;</div>\n            <div class=\"item active\">System Event Settings &#9662;</div>\n            <div class=\"item\" style=\"padding-left:26px;\">Event/Action</div>\n            <div class=\"item\" style=\"padding-left:26px;\">Alarm In</div>\n            <div class=\"item\" style=\"padding-left:26px;\">Virtual Alarm In</div>\n            <div class=\"item\" style=\"padding-left:26px;\">Tamper Detection</div>\n            <div class=\"item\" style=\"padding-left:26px;\">External Alarm Box</div>\n            <div class=\"item active\" style=\"padding-left:26px;\">Disarm</div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"app-main\">\n            <div class=\"app-breadcrumb\">Home / App Settings / System Event Settings / Disarm</div>\n            <div class=\"app-h\">Disarm</div>\n            <div class=\"app-panel\">\n              <strong style=\"font-size:12.5px;\">Arm/Disarm Instant Settings &#9432;</strong>\n              <div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:14px;margin-top:12px;font-size:12px;\">\n                <div><div style=\"margin-bottom:6px;\">All</div><span class=\"btn small\">Arm</span> <span class=\"btn small\">Disarm</span></div>\n                <div><div style=\"margin-bottom:6px;\">CH 1</div><span class=\"btn small\">Arm</span> <span class=\"btn small\">Disarm</span></div>\n                <div><div style=\"margin-bottom:6px;\">CH 2</div><span class=\"btn small\">Arm</span> <span class=\"btn small\">Disarm</span></div>\n                <div><div style=\"margin-bottom:6px;\">CH 3</div><span class=\"btn small\">Arm</span> <span class=\"btn small\">Disarm</span></div>\n              </div>\n              <div style=\"margin-top:14px;font-size:12px;\">\n                <div style=\"margin-bottom:6px;\">System Event Action Rule</div><span class=\"btn small\">Arm</span> <span class=\"btn small\">Disarm</span>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"app-panel\">\n              <div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;margin-bottom:12px;\"><strong style=\"font-size:12.5px;\">Arm/Disarm Rules</strong><span class=\"btn small primary\">+ Add Rule</span></div>\n              <table class=\"app-table\">\n                <tr><th>Rule Name</th><th>Activation</th><th>Handler</th><th>Set Arm/Disarm Status</th><th>Apply To Channels</th><th>Operation</th></tr>\n              </table>\n              <div style=\"text-align:center;color:var(--text-muted);font-size:12px;padding:16px 0;\">No items &#8856;</div>\n            </div>\n            <div style=\"background:#eef2fd;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 14px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;font-size:12px;\">\n              <span>To save AI app configurations as multiple presets and switch between them all at once, enable AI app preset mode.</span>\n              <span class=\"btn small primary\">Enable AI App Preset Mode</span>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <figcaption>Disarm page \u2014 Enable AI App Preset Mode</figcaption>\n      </div>\n\n      <p>On the Disarm page, click <strong>Enable AI App Preset Mode</strong> to turn on preset mode. Any AI apps that were already configured are registered under the <strong>Arm</strong> preset and continue to work as before. Once preset mode is enabled, the Disarm page is replaced with the AI App Preset settings page.</p>\n\n      <h2>Switching AI App Presets</h2>\n      <p>Use the <span style=\"display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;\"><span class=\"btn small\">&#9675; Arm</span><span class=\"btn small primary\">&#9899; Disarm</span></span> button in the top header to switch the active arm/disarm preset. After selecting the preset you want and confirming, a progress indicator shows while the preset is applied; once complete, the AI apps registered to that preset become active.</p>\n\n      <div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:420px;\">\n        <div class=\"modal-mock\">\n          <div class=\"modal-head\">Applying Preset Settings</div>\n          <div class=\"modal-body\">\n            <div class=\"usage-bar\" style=\"height:10px;margin-bottom:8px;\"><span style=\"width:50%;\"></span></div>\n            <p style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);text-align:center;margin:0;\">This may take up to 30 seconds. Please wait.</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n        <figcaption>Applying preset settings</figcaption>\n      </div>\n\n      <h2>Switching Presets with an Alarm Input</h2>\n      <div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:520px;\">\n        <div class=\"app-panel\">\n          <p style=\"font-size:12.5px;margin:0 0 10px;\">Switch presets by alarm input</p>\n          <p style=\"font-size:11.5px;color:var(--text-muted);margin:0 0 10px;\">When alarm input is On, it automatically switches to the &lsquo;Disarm&rsquo; preset; when Off, it switches to the &lsquo;Arm&rsquo; preset.</p>\n          <select disabled style=\"width:160px;\"><option>None</option><option>Alarm In 1</option><option>Alarm In 2</option><option>Alarm In 3</option><option>Alarm In 4</option></select>\n        </div>\n        <figcaption>Switch presets by alarm input</figcaption>\n      </div>\n      <p>The preset switches automatically based on the state of the selected alarm input. When the alarm input is On, it syncs to the <strong>Disarm</strong> preset; when Off, it syncs to the <strong>Arm</strong> preset. Click <strong>Save</strong> after changing the value to apply it.</p>\n      <p>Because an alarm input signal is only On/Off, this doesn't work once there are three or more AI app presets, including the default Arm/Disarm presets. Deleting an added AI app preset lets you configure this again, and it resumes automatically once an alarm input is selected.</p>\n      <p><strong>If linked to an alarm input, the preset can't be changed from the web page or via the API.</strong></p>\n\n      <h2>Adding an AI App Preset</h2>\n      <div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:600px;\">\n        <div class=\"app-panel\">\n          <div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;margin-bottom:8px;\"><strong style=\"font-size:12.5px;\">AI App Preset List &nbsp;<span style=\"color:var(--text-muted);font-weight:400;\">3/4</span></strong><span class=\"btn small primary\">+ Add</span></div>\n          <p style=\"font-size:11px;color:var(--text-muted);margin:0 0 12px;\">The AI apps in the active preset will run. You can change the active preset from the top header.</p>\n          <div style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--blue);padding-left:10px;margin-bottom:10px;\">\n            <div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:12px;\"><span>Arm &nbsp;<span class=\"badge\">Current Active Preset</span></span><span class=\"btn small\">+ Add AI App</span></div>\n            <div style=\"font-size:11px;color:var(--text-muted);margin-top:6px;\">AI Engine Resource &#9432; 408 / 1000</div>\n            <div class=\"usage-bar\" style=\"height:8px;margin:4px 0;\"><span style=\"width:41%;\"></span></div>\n            <div style=\"font-size:11px;color:var(--text-muted);\">Active AI Apps: Heatmap, Stay &amp; Go, Stopping Detection, Zone Counting</div>\n          </div>\n          <div style=\"margin-bottom:10px;\">\n            <div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:12px;\"><span>Disarm</span><span class=\"btn small\" style=\"opacity:.5;\">Delete</span></div>\n            <div style=\"font-size:11px;color:var(--text-muted);margin-top:6px;\">AI Engine Resource &#9432; 204 / 1000</div>\n            <div class=\"usage-bar\" style=\"height:8px;margin:4px 0;\"><span style=\"width:20%;\"></span></div>\n            <div style=\"font-size:11px;color:var(--text-muted);\">Active AI Apps: Thermal Intrusion Detection</div>\n          </div>\n          <div style=\"border-left:3px solid #d64545;padding-left:10px;\">\n            <div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:12px;\"><span>Preset 3 &#9998;</span><span class=\"btn small\">Delete</span></div>\n            <div style=\"font-size:11px;color:var(--text-muted);margin-top:6px;\">AI Engine Resource &#9432; 0 / 1000</div>\n            <div class=\"usage-bar\" style=\"height:8px;margin:4px 0;\"></div>\n            <div style=\"font-size:11px;color:var(--text-muted);\">Active AI Apps: No AI apps are available to run when enabled.</div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n        <figcaption>AI App Preset List</figcaption>\n      </div>\n      <ol>\n        <li>On the AI App Preset settings screen, click the <span class=\"btn small primary\">+ Add</span> button in the <strong>AI App Preset List</strong> area to add an AI app preset.</li>\n        <li>A newly added AI app preset starts with no AI apps assigned. Presets you add beyond the two default presets (Arm / Disarm) can be renamed using the edit (&#9998;) button.</li>\n      </ol>\n      <p>Up to four presets can be configured. Once you've added a preset beyond the two default presets (Arm/Disarm) \u2014 three or more total \u2014 the header's <span style=\"display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;\"><span class=\"btn small\">&#9675; Arm</span><span class=\"btn small primary\">&#9899; Disarm</span></span> button changes as shown below.</p>\n\n      <h2>Adding AI Apps to a Preset</h2>\n      <ol>\n        <li>Click the header's <span style=\"display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;\"><span class=\"btn small\">&#9675; Arm</span><span class=\"btn small primary\">&#9899; Disarm</span></span> button to activate the preset you want to add AI apps to. With three or more presets configured beyond the default Arm/Disarm presets, a list appears \u2014 click the preset you want, then confirm to activate it.</li>\n        <li>The currently active AI app preset shows an <strong>Add AI App</strong> button. Clicking it takes you to the <strong>Explore AI Apps</strong> page \u2014 configuring AI apps there, per the <a href=\"/application-guide\">Application User Guide</a>, adds them to the current active preset.</li>\n        <li>Even without clicking that button, navigating to <strong>Explore AI Apps</strong> and configuring AI apps per the <a href=\"/application-guide\">Application User Guide</a> adds them to the current active preset.</li>\n      </ol>\n      <p>Each AI app preset's AI Engine gauge shows the combined processing load required by the AI apps registered to that preset, relative to the maximum load the AI Bridge can handle. Since different AI apps require different amounts of AI processing, be careful not to configure a preset that exceeds the maximum load.</p>\n\n      <h2>Deleting an AI App Preset</h2>\n      <p>Any AI app preset other than the default Arm/Disarm presets can be deleted by clicking <strong>Delete</strong> and confirming. Deleting a preset resets the AI app configuration it contained. If you delete the currently active preset, the Arm preset becomes active.</p>\n\n      <h2>Disabling AI App Preset Mode</h2>\n      <p>Click the <strong>Disable AI App Preset Mode</strong> button at the bottom of the AI App Preset settings page to turn preset mode off. Once disabled, the device runs based on the AI apps configured under the Arm preset. Your configured AI app presets are saved, and become available again if you re-enable AI app preset mode.</p>\n      <p>Disabling AI app preset mode switches the AI App Preset settings page back to the Disarm page.</p>";
